From: boa-z <boa-z@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: use CSR_SATP instead of the obsolete sptbr alias

Modern binutils rejects sptbr. Use the existing CSR_SATP constant
for the same register (0x180) during address-space switches.

Signed-off-by: boa-z <boa-z@outlook.com>
---
--- a/arch/riscv/mm/context.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/mm/context.c
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@
 	asid = (next->context.asid.counter & SATP_ASID_MASK)
 		<< SATP_ASID_SHIFT;
 
-	csr_write(sptbr, virt_to_pfn(next->pgd) | SATP_MODE | asid);
+	csr_write(CSR_SATP, virt_to_pfn(next->pgd) | SATP_MODE | asid);
 #endif
 
 	flush_icache_deferred(next);
